# Never Revert Local Changes

RULE: Never run git reset --hard, git clean -fd, git restore, or checkout that discards uncommitted work without explicit user request.
WHY: Parallel agents or branch switches can permanently lose hours of work.
CODEX: 06-coding-standards/README.md

DO:
  git status first; if changes exist, ask user: stash, commit, or cancel
  git stash push -u -m "Save work" before switching branches

NEVER:
  git reset --hard
  git clean -fd
  git checkout <branch> when uncommitted changes exist
